HLPROT {
[1;36mThe [1;37mROTATE[1;36m command will cause the directional thrusters to rotate the ship a
specified number of degrees, or to a specified heading. If you specify an
absolute heading, the ship will automatically turn in the direction which
causes the shortest arc to arrive at the given heading. Issue the command as
follows:

[1;37m  rotate [1;32m[degrees]
[1;36m      or
[1;37m  rotate @[1;32m[heading]

[1;32m  degrees [1;36m= degrees to rotate to port (negative) or starboard (positive)
[1;32m  heading [1;36m= the absolute direction regardless of your current heading

  examples: [1;37mrotate 5   [1;36mturns the ship 5 degrees to the starboard (right)
            [1;37mrotate -5  [1;36mturns the ship 5 degrees to the port (left)
            [1;37mrot @5     [1;36mturns the ship to 5 degrees absolute
[1;37m} T GE help rotate message

HLPSET {
[1;36mThe [1;37mSET[1;36m command lets you set user-configurable options. Issue the command as
follows:

[1;37m  set [1;32m[option/[1;37m?[1;32m] [setting]
[1;36m
  [1;32moptions[1;36m:
[1;37m    scan [1;36m-- change SCAN SE/RA display
[1;37m       simple       [1;36m-- display maps only
[1;37m       full         [1;36m-- display maps with list of ships or planets
[1;37m       fullnames    [1;36m-- include ship names in list on second line
[1;37m       fullextra    [1;36m-- include more than 8 ships if necessary
[1;37m       nomap        [1;36m-- do not display map, text only

[1;37m    display [1;36m-- adjust messages shown
[1;36mEnter [1;37mHELP SET2[1;36m for more information on display filters.

[1;36mEnter [1;37mSET ?[1;36m to show a list of options and their current settings.

Examples:
