[1;37m} T GE help set2 message

HLPSCA {
[1;36mThe [1;37mSCAN[1;36m command displays information from your ship's tactical scanners. Issue
the command as follows:

[1;37m  scan [1;32m[type] [ship letter/planet number/range]

[1;32mtype[1;36m:
  [1;37msh[1;36m = ship scan showing detail on [1;32mship letter
  [1;37mpl[1;36m = planet scan showing detail on [1;32mplanet number
  [1;37mse[1;36m = sector scan showing the ships, planets, and mines in this sector
  [1;37mra[1;36m = close range scan showing ships and mines
     [1;32mrange 1 to 9[1;36m can be specified, with 9 being full range, and the rest
     shrinking quadratically. Alternatively, [1;32mh[1;36m can be specified for half range,
     and [1;32mq[1;36m for one quarter range.
  [1;37mlo[1;36m = long range scan (10x) showing ships
     [1;32mh[1;36m can be specified for half range, and [1;32mq[1;36m for one quarter range.

[1;36mExamples: [1;37mscan se            scan sh a
          scan sh @          scan pl 1
          sca ra             sca ra 4
          sca lo             sca lo q

[1;36mSee the [1;37mSET[1;36m command for additional configuration options for [1;37mSCAN[1;36m.[1;37m
} T GE help scan message

HLPSEN {
[1;36mUse the [1;37mSEND[1;36m command to communicate with other ships and team members. Issue
the command as follows:

  [1;37msend [1;32m[type] [message]

  [1;32mtype [1;36m= [A]LL, [T]EAM, or [E]NCODED

ALL messages are sent on all standard hyperspace hailing frequencies and will
be received by all ships in the galaxy. You can also use the [1;37m>[1;36m shortcut.

TEAM messages will be received by all ships belonging to members of your team;
you must be on a team to use this.

ENCODED messages will be received only by ships that have their communications
module tuned to the same hyperspace frequency. Use [1;37mSEND FREQ [1;32mxxxxx[1;36m to set the
current ship's frequency. Valid frequencies are 1-65535; set to 0 to turn off.
[1;37mSEND FREQ[1;36m by itself will display the current frequency.

Examples: [1;37msend A This is a warning to all ships, I am here!
          sen TEAM OK, now is the time to strike!
          sen E No one else can know about this secret!
          send FREQ 38146
          > What's up everyone

Use [1;37m>[1;36m to chat in the lobby.
} T GE help send message

HLPSHI {
[1;36mThe [1;37mSHIELD[1;36m command will raise or lower the ship's shields. The shields will
begin charging upon being raised for the first time. They provide immediate yet
limited protection until fully charged. When fully charged, the shields come up
immediately when issued. The shields do drain on the neutron flux pile, and
will automatically come down when the energy drops to dangerously low levels.
Issue the command as follows:

  [1;37mshield [1;32m[[1;37mup[1;32m/[1;37mdown[1;32m]

[1;36mWhen firing a weapon with the shields up, the shields will be automatically
lowered. They WILL NOT be automatically raised after the firing.
[1;37m} T GE help shield message

HLPTOR {
[1;36mThe [1;37mTORPEDO[1;36m command fires a torpedo at a given ship. The torpedo guidance
system will attempt to lock on the ship prior to firing the torpedo. If a lock
is made, the torpedo is launched.

Issue the command as follows:

  [1;37mtorpedo [1;32m[ship letter/[1;37m@[1;32m]

  [1;32mship letter[1;36m = the ship you are firing upon
  [1;37m@[1;36m = to fire at the locked on ship

  examples: [1;37mtorpedo A   [1;36mfires a torpedo at ship A.
            [1;37mtor @       [1;36mfires at the ship you locked on with the [1;37mLOCK[1;36m cmd

Type [1;37mHELP BATTLE[1;36m for more information on torpedoes.
[1;37m} T GE help torpedo message

HLPTRA {
[1;36mThe [1;37mTRANSFER[1;36m command permits you to transfer goods from your ship to a planet
or from a planet to your ship.

To transfer up, simply use the command [1;37mTRANSFER UP[1;36m. This will transfer
up everything on the planet and install any usable upgrades.

If you wish to transfer anything down to a planet:

[1;37m  transfer [1;32m[[1;37md(own)[1;32m] [([1;37m-[1;32m)amount/[1;37mall[1;32m] [item]

  amount[1;36m = the amount to transfer (use - sign for all but this amount)
           [1;37mall[1;36m to transfer down all onboard

  [1;32mitem[1;36m:
[1;37m    mis [1;36m= transfer missiles     [1;37mmin [1;36m= transfer mines
[1;37m    tor [1;36m= transfer torpedoes    [1;37mjam [1;36m= transfer jammers
[1;37m    dec [1;36m= transfer decoys       [1;37mzip [1;36m= transfer zippers
[1;37m    flu [1;36m= transfer flux pods    [1;37mgol [1;36m= transfer gold

} T GE help transfer message

HLPWAR {
[1;36mThe [1;37mWARP[1;36m command starts the warp drives (provided your type of ship has them)
and directs your course and speed. Issue the command as follows:

  [1;37mwarp [1;32m[speed] [degrees/[1;37m@[1;32mheading]

  [1;32mspeed [1;36m= the warp speed
  [1;32mdegrees [1;36m= degrees to rotate to port (negative) or starboard (positive)
  [1;32mheading [1;36m= the absolute direction regardless of your current heading

Examples: [1;37mwarp 5     [1;36malters the speed to warp 5 and does not change the heading
          [1;37mwarp 10 5  [1;36malters the speed to warp 10 and turns the ship 5 degrees
                     to the starboard (right).
          [1;37mwar 20 -10 [1;36malters the speed to warp 20 and turns the ship 10 degrees
                     to the port (left).
          [1;37mwar 8 @90  [1;36malters the speed to warp 8 and turns the ship to 90
                     degrees absolute.
[1;37m} T GE help warp message

HLPSTAT {
[1;36mThe [1;37mSTATUS[1;36m command displays the current arena status and player list.

In the lobby, STATUS shows which players are ready, observing, or serving as
host, along with any automatic-start countdown.

During a match, STATUS shows the time remaining and whether each player is
playing or observing. Scoring for the current mode is shown as well.
[1;37m} T GE help status message

HLPSTO {
[1;36mThe [1;37mSTOP[1;36m command cuts the engines and brings your ship to a complete stop, even
if your ship's helm is damaged and not accepting commands.
[1;37m} T GE help stop message


HLPZIP {
[1;36mThe [1;37mZIPPER[1;36m command launches a defensive (and sometimes offensive) weapon which
interferes with the timing mechanism on mines. The effect is to trip all mines
in the vicinity of the player's ship into exploding immediately. This weapon
can trip an opponent's mines after they have laid them but before they can
distance themself from them, causing the mines to do damage to the
opponent's own ship.
[1;37m} T GE help zipper message

